            <ArticleTitle>[A man with a painful chest after frequent vomiting].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A1183</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-year-old man presented with chest pain and weight loss, starting after a period of vomiting. Contrast radiography of the esophagus revealed an esophageal-pleural fistula. The patient was successfully treated by stent placement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
